id: E14723
trigger_tool: make|conan
phase: testing
error_signature: Faketime or datefudge missing|datefudge: not found|tst_usersfile.sh.*FAIL
severity: 2
category: autotools, testing, build-requirements
match_keywords: datefudge, FAKETIME, make check, build_requirements, test helper, time-dependent test
title: Upstream time-dependent tests need their clock helper in the build context
root_cause: An Automake test script invokes an external clock-control command at test runtime. The production library can compile without it, but the complete upstream suite cannot run. A host-side shell installation or a target runtime requirement is not a reproducible Conan build-context declaration.
affected_scope: Native target builds with upstream tests invoking external date or clock virtualization utilities; not a rule to fake results or to replace upstream test cases.
verification_cmd: conan create archives/o/oath/2.6.14 -pr:h ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=missing; inspect liboath/tests and oathtool/tests Automake summaries
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: declare-test-helper-in-build-context
rec_description: Inventory upstream test scripts and their subprocess commands before reporting the denominator. Declare the exact published clock helper as a Conan build requirement, keep the script and its assertions intact, then run the complete registered suite and verify each terminal PASS record.
rec_command: Add the exact helper reference in build_requirements(), then run make check -j1 in the target Conan build.
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: manual
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: hold-submission-until-helper-available
fallback_description: If the helper is unavailable on the target, leave the upstream suite unverified and stop the PR gate; do not count missing-tool diagnostics as a test pass or silently shrink the denominator.
fallback_command: Check the exact helper package and target executable before retrying the unchanged upstream tests.
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: missing.*datefudge.*(PASS|skip.*acceptable)
forbid_1_reason: A missing runtime test tool is not evidence that the underlying behavior passed.
forbid_1_consequence: Inflated upstream pass rate or understated test inventory.
